  "notes": "From English \"open.\" Very common and versatile in modern Japanese.\n\nSENSE 1 — BUSINESS OPENING:\nUsed for new shops, restaurants, and facilities. Often seen on banners and advertisements.\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- グランドオープン: grand opening\n- プレオープン: pre-opening, soft opening\n- リニューアルオープン: reopening after renovation\n- {新規|しんき}オープン: newly opened\n\nSENSE 2 — OPEN/TRANSPARENT:\nFunctions as a na-adjective (オープンな) and adverb (オープンに).\n- オープンキャンパス: open campus (university open day)\n- オープンカー: convertible car\n- オープンスペース: open space",
